Trace all six string drawer paths, not two.

cocotron 0142 traced sizeOfString: and drawString:withAttributes:inRect:, and its commit message
concluded that a Money Manager Ex weekday label reading Wednesda is drawn by some route outside
NSStringDrawer entirely. THAT CONCLUSION WAS WRONG and this is the patch that shows it.

NSStringDrawer has SIX entry points, not the two that were traced:

    sizeOfString:withAttributes:inSize:              traced by 0142
    drawString:withAttributes:inRect:                traced by 0142
    drawString:withAttributes:atPoint:inSize:        NOT traced
    sizeOfAttributedString:inSize:                   traced already, CIDER_TRACE_TEXT
    drawAttributedString:inRect:                     NOT traced
    drawAttributedString:atPoint:inSize:             NOT traced

With all six printing, the same drive answers immediately:

    CIDER_MEASURE drawAttrRect "Wednesday" len=9 inRect=64.00x14.00@2.00,0.00

So it goes through drawAttributedString:inRect:, which is one of the three I had left dark, and
the earlier silence meant only that I had instrumented the wrong half.

AND THE NUMBERS NOW LINE UP. sizeOfAttributedString: answers 65.00 for that same nine character
string, and the draw is given a rect 64.00 wide. One point short, and the last glyph is not placed
at all rather than drawn clipped, which is exactly the capture: eight complete glyphs and then
blank space where the ninth belongs.

What that one point means is NOT settled here. Either the measurement over reports and the width
the caller derived from it is right, or the caller narrows what it was told and our layout then
drops a glyph macOS would have clipped. Both are testable and neither is tested yet, so this patch
claims only the measurement.

Counts from that drive, so the instrument can be seen to be alive on every path that fired: 53
sizeOfString, 51 drawString inRect, 135 drawAttributedString inRect.

--- a/AppKit/NSStringDrawer.m
+++ b/AppKit/NSStringDrawer.m
@@ -160,6 +160,15 @@
 {
     NSRange glyphRange;
 
+    /* Same switch as the other paths. Instrumenting two of the SIX entry points here produced a
+     * confident wrong claim about where a label is drawn, so all of them print. */
+    if (getenv("CIDER_TRACE_MEASURE") != NULL) {
+        fprintf(stderr, "CIDER_MEASURE drawAt \"%.40s\" len=%lu at=%.2f,%.2f max=%.0f\n",
+                [string UTF8String] ?: "(nil)", (unsigned long) [string length], point.x, point.y,
+                maxSize.width);
+        fflush(stderr);
+    }
+
     if (maxSize.width == NSZeroSize.width &&
         maxSize.height == NSZeroSize.height)
         maxSize = NSMakeSize(NSStringDrawerLargeDimension,
@@ -258,6 +267,13 @@
 {
     NSRange glyphRange;
 
+    if (getenv("CIDER_TRACE_MEASURE") != NULL) {
+        fprintf(stderr, "CIDER_MEASURE drawAttrRect \"%.40s\" len=%lu inRect=%.2fx%.2f@%.2f,%.2f\n",
+                [[astring string] UTF8String] ?: "(nil)", (unsigned long) [astring length],
+                rect.size.width, rect.size.height, rect.origin.x, rect.origin.y);
+        fflush(stderr);
+    }
+
     [_textContainer setContainerSize: rect.size];
     [_textStorage setAttributedString: astring];
 
